{"repositoryId":1251731739,"availability":"available","full":"nextjs/next-beats","name":"next-beats","description":"A Next.js 16.3 music player demo showcasing Instant Navigations with Cache Components and Partial Prefetching.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":168,"forks":30,"created":"2026-05-27T21:32:27Z","updated":"2026-10-14T00:49:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://next-beats.dev","topics":["cache-components","demo","instant-navigation","music-player","nextjs","prefetching","react","streaming","tailwindcss","typescript","vgpu"],"demo":"https://next-beats.dev/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:58.108Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:58.108Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:58.108Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T21:46:58.108Z","stars":168,"forks":30}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Next.js 16.3 music player demo showcasing Instant Navigations."],"features":["Cache Components cache each query with 'use cache', name the data with cacheTag, and set its lifetime with cacheLife, so repeated reads come from the cache until a tag is invalidated.","Partial Prefetching prefetches one shared App Shell per route. Links with prefetch={true} also resolve dynamic params and searchParams, including the cached content behind them while uncached data streams after…","Hover-triggered prefetch delays URL-specific prefetches in long track lists until the pointer or focus reaches a link, avoiding a separate prefetch for every destination in view.","Server Functions run mutations such as favoriting a track or creating a playlist on the server, and invalidate only the tags they change with updateTag, which re-prefetches the affected routes so they stay instant and…","React Compiler memoizes components and hooks automatically, so the code needs no manual useMemo or useCallback."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nextjs/next-beats/blob/main/README.m